system "ISO:san-Deva:Latn:15919-2026" {

metadata {
  authority_id iso
  id 15919-2026
  language iso-639-2:san
  source_script Deva
  destination_script Latn
  name "ISO/DIS 15919 (2026) Information and documentation -- Transliteration of Indic scripts into Latin characters (Sanskrit; DIS stage)"
  url https://www.iso.org/committee/48820.html
  creation_date 2026
  adoption_date 2026
  description {    Second edition (DIS stage) of ISO 15919, Transliteration of Indic scripts into Latin characters.
    Encoded from the committee ballot ISO/TC 46/WG 3 N125; per-script tables of clause 7,
    numerals of normative Annex A, Rule 17 Vedic accents, and options 9.8/9.9/9.10 as
    selectable variants (languages opt98 opt99 opt10). See notes for provenance and errata.  }

  notes {
    note "Encoded from ISO/DIS 15919 (2026), ISO/TC 46/WG 3 N125 (DIS stage draft, 2026-01-26), Table 7.1 plus the numerals of normative Annex A Table A.2; shared-table content verified against ISO/CD 15919 (2025, N108) and ISO 15919 WD (2024, N88). The DIS is not yet a published International Standard."
    note "Rule 2 convention: inherent a with a consonant is always transliterated (consonant rows carry the inherent a)."
    note "virama is deleted in the default behavior (clause 6 printed virama hex list); option 9.10 (language selector opt10) instead renders virama as middle dot U+00B7."
    note "Option selectors (W3 languages, single-select): opt98 = clause 9.8 upper-case for all initial vowels (first letter capitalised for digraph outputs); opt99 = clause 9.9 unusual conjuncts marked with equals sign U+003D via the script's zero-width joiner; opt10 = clause 9.10 explicit virama middle dot. Option 9.1 (non-uniform e/o) is available by character substitution on outputs and is not separately staged."
    note "Rule 17: the Vedic accents jihvamuliya (Hex 1CF5, Devanagari ᳵ) and upadhmaniya (Hex 1CF6, Devanagari ᳶ) are transliterated ẖ (Hex 1E96) and ḫ (Hex 1E2B). Table 7.1 itself does not print these rows (its NOTE defers Vedic accents to Rules 13 and 17 of 8.1), so they are encoded here from Rule 17. The r̆ rows cover the printed ṟa+virāma letter (0931 094D) and the ra+virāma+zero-width-joiner sequence of Table 7.1 footnote b (0930 094D 200D)."
    note "Cross-check (audit axis): Wikipedia ISO 15919 table (2001-reflected) vs corpus map agreement 57/75 printed rows; systematic divergences recorded as findings, not fixes: vocalic r/l rows (corpus ṛ-family vs ISO r̥-family), long e/o rows (corpus e/o vs ISO ē/ō), avagraha (corpus :’ vs ISO ')."
  }
}

languages opt98 opt99 opt10

tests {
   "अ" ->  "a"
   "क" ->  "ka"
   "आ" ->  "ā"
   "ा" ->  "ā"
   "ख" ->  "kha"
   "इ" ->  "i"
   "ि" ->  "i"
